From 3ce54d4df55aab60f4b6513d448a3c4e69468d9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Metroid Bring-up <metroid@localhost>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: audio: let device own the VINTF version

Nothing Phone (3) stock B4.1 registers the Bluetooth audio provider as
AIDL version 4 from audiohalservice.qti. The source implementation installs
an AIDL version 5 fragment for the same instance, causing a conflicting
FqInstance when both are selected.

Keep the source library available, but let the device-specific stock v4
fragment be the sole manifest owner.
---
 bluetooth/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bluetooth/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp b/bluetooth/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp
--- a/bluetooth/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp
+++ b/bluetooth/audio/aidl/default/Android.bp
@@ -10,7 +10,6 @@ package {
 cc_library_shared {
     name: "android.hardware.bluetooth.audio-impl",
     vendor: true,
-    vintf_fragments: ["bluetooth_audio.xml"],
     defaults: [
         "aconfig_lib_cc_static_link.defaults",
         "latest_android_hardware_bluetooth_audio_ndk_shared",
-- 
2.43.0

